Q: Difference between 2 numbers A: <pre><code>namespace Sys
{
    public static class Math
    {
        // Absolute delta value function returns unsigned result (without  overflows).


        /// &lt;summary&gt;Absolute delta value |b - a|.&lt;/summary&gt;
        [MethodImpl(MethodImplOptions.AggressiveInlining)] // For framework
        public static uint AbsDelta(int a, int b)
        {
            return (a &lt;= b) ? (uint)b - (uint)a : (uint)a - (uint)b;
        }

        /// &lt;summary&gt;Absolute delta value |b - a|.&lt;/summary&gt;
        [MethodImpl(MethodImplOptions.AggressiveInlining)] // For framework
        public static uint AbsDelta(uint a, uint b)
        {
            return (a &lt;= b) ? b - a : a - b;
        }

        /// &lt;summary&gt;Absolute delta value |b - a|.&lt;/summary&gt;
        [MethodImpl(MethodImplOptions.AggressiveInlining)] // For framework
        public static ulong AbsDelta(long a, long b)
        {
            return (a &lt;= b) ? (ulong)b - (ulong)a : (ulong)a - (ulong)b;
        }

        /// &lt;summary&gt;Absolute delta value |b - a|.&lt;/summary&gt;
        [MethodImpl(MethodImplOptions.AggressiveInlining)] // For framework
        public static ulong AbsDelta(ulong a, ulong b)
        {
            return (a &lt;= b) ? b - a : a - b;
        }
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>P.s. Authors question for decimals, but question for not decimals here [closed]:<br />
<a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/1111194/c-sharp-function-to-find-the-delta-of-two-numbers">Function to find the delta of two numbers [duplicate]</a></p>

Q: How can we use constant variables as data members of a class? A: <p>Why not? You can write</p>

<pre><code>class A {
  const int i = 0;
};
</code></pre>

<p>or</p>

<pre><code>class A {
const int i = 0;
public:
  A() {}
  A(int j) : i(j) {}
};
</code></pre>
